c. service centers and safe houses;and/ord. other facilities and infrastructure necessary for the recovery of victims.
3. The provision of services to victims of acts of violence is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with P2TP2A and other social institutions;
4. P2TP2A and other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (3) may receive and send case referrals from other service units in a networked manner;
5. Integrated services for victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) through (4) are implemented in accordance with standard operating procedures;
6. Provisions regarding Standard Operating Procedures as referred to in paragraph (5) are regulated by Governor Regulation.

CHAPTER X

GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 29

1. The Regional Government carries out guidance and supervision of FP2ATK and other social institutions;
2. Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be by the Regional Apparatus implementing women and child empowerment affairs;
3. The results of the implementation of guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (2) must be reported to the regional government.

Article 17

1. The Regional Government conducts cooperation and coordination in order to ensure the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence;
2. Cooperation and coordination as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

Article 14

1. Protection of children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in article 6 letter a is the responsibility of the Regional Government;
2. Protection of children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by:a. formulating policies for prevention, reduction of vulnerable risks, handling of victims and child data and information systems;
b. organizing maintenance, care, and social rehabilitation of neglected children, both within and outside institutions;
c. providing shelter, maintenance and care for neglected children; and organizing special protection for children.

Article 15 (1) Provisions regarding prevention and services for acts of violence and protection of women as referred to in Articles 7 through Article 13 apply mutatis mutandis to the protection of children from acts of violence;

2. In addition to carrying out prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), also by means of increasing family capacity in child protection and child-rearing skills.

Article 22

1. The Regional Government in the context of services for victims of acts of violence, establishes P2TP2A;
2. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) has the duties to:  a. provide services, including:
1. receive complaints/reports of violence against women and/or children, consultation, and counseling;
2. receive and send case referrals from Regency/City Regional Government or institutions established by Regency/City Regional Government;
3. provide legal assistance and support;
4. health;
5. social rehabilitation;
6. legal services;and
7. repatriation and social reintegration.  b. provide protection to victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses.
3. The appointment of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) is stipulated by Regent Decree.
4. Regional Apparatus conducts guidance for P2TP2A in carrying out duties as referred to in paragraph (2).

Article 9

1. The Regional Government carries out prevention as referred to in Article 5 letter a by:
a. socializing laws and regulations;
b. providing counseling/guidance;
c. providing education on the dangers of domestic violence;
d. conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
e. forming work networks in violence prevention efforts;
f. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
g. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping locations or areas prone to violence; and
h. increasing public awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms.
2. In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. social community institutions; and
f. business world and other institutions.

Article 18

1. The Regional Government in conducting cooperation and coordination for the Protection of Women and children from acts of violence, establishes FP2ATK;
2. FP2ATK membership consists of elements of:a. regional government;
b. vertical agencies;
c. educational institutions;andd. community organizations concerned with the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
3. The Organizational Structure of FP2ATK as referred to in paragraph (2) consists of:a. policy formulation working group;
b. socialization working group;
c. service working group;andd. data, information, monitoring and evaluation working group.  (4) The establishment and term of office of FP2ATK members as referred to in paragraph (1), is stipulated by Regent Decree.
